---
/**
 * Renderer for Tina rich-text `html` / `html_inline` nodes.
 *
 * TinaMarkdown's built-in handling for those node types interpolates `value`
 * as an Astro expression, which HTML-escapes it — pre-rendered markup lands on
 * the page as visible `&lt;pre&gt;…` source text. Every Shiki-highlighted code
 * block arrives as an `html` node (see RichText.astro), so without this
 * override no code block on the site renders.
 *
 * TRUST: today every value is either this site's own Shiki output or raw HTML an
 * author committed to this repo, which the MDX pipeline also rendered unescaped
 * (astro.config.ts sets no rehype-sanitize). So this does not widen anything as
 * things stand.
 *
 * It WILL widen in phase 4. Once Tina Cloud lets someone edit a post without a
 * commit and a review, an `html` block containing a <script> becomes stored XSS
 * on every visitor. Highlighter output cannot simply be given its own node type
 * to separate the two — @tinacms/astro's Node.astro dispatches a fixed set of
 * types and drops anything else — so the split has to happen another way, e.g.
 * routing author HTML through an allowlist sanitiser while the highlighter feeds
 * a component override directly. Resolve that before Tina Cloud writes go live.
 */
interface Props {
	value: string;
}

const { value } = Astro.props;
---

<Fragment set:html={value} />
